From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: mux UART2 on header pins 11 and 13

The 26-pin header exposes XGPIOB[11]/[12], which are pads VIVO_D10 and
VIVO_D9. According to the official SG2000 pinout table, UART2_TX/RX is
function 7 on those pads; the dedicated UART2_TX/RX pads (K15/K13) are a
different ball pair and are not wired to this header.

Muxing K15/K13 therefore left pins 11/13 idle: the UART controller ran,
stty accepted the baud, but nothing reached the modem (RX stayed 0 even
with 11-13 shorted).

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -146,6 +146,18 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/* Header pins 11/13 are XGPIOB[11]/[12] (pads VIVO_D10/VIVO_D9);
+	 * UART2_TX/RX is mux 7 there, not the dedicated K15/K13 pads. */
+	uart2_cfg: uart2-cfg {
+		uart2-pins {
+			pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_VIVO_D10, 7)>,
+				 <PINMUX(PIN_VIVO_D9, 7)>;
+			bias-pull-up;
+			drive-strength-microamp = <10800>;
+			power-source = <3300>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	sdhci1_cfg: sdhci1-cfg {
 		/* Vendor U-Boot cvi_sdio1_pad_setting: CLK pull-down, CMD/DAT
 		 * pull-up, drive strength left at the weakest default. */
@@ -316,6 +328,8 @@
  * and the UART card in Settings shows it. UART1 is muxed by S31slip; the
  * other pads need a board-specific fmux setup before use. */
 &uart2 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2_cfg>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 

